A||||9||fropuff||Is kph to mph a problem?||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||04-08-2000||04:46 PM||||I found a very nice '85 Fiero GT for sale in Ontario, and my question is if it is hard to convert from kph to mph.  I know I will have to recalibrate, but that's about it.  Do you know where I can find some used speedometers for sale?  (Some so that I don't have to turn them back...it's illegal ya know).||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||04-08-2000||04:59 PM||||There are more thing to worry about than a KPH dash. You should make sure it passes local emmisions.<P>Actually If you do the killometer to mile math for the conversion and set the mph dash to the same "milage" as the kph dash there is nothing illegal about it. Save the old kph dash some place in case anyone ever wants to check. It's simple bit of math on any caclulator but I don't remember it right now.<P>Most states do have allowance for replacing the dash anyway. In most states it's as simple as stating on the bill of sale that the odo was replaced and doesn't reflect real miles. Changing the odometer is only illegal if you fail to tell the buyer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||04-08-2000||05:05 PM||||Does that mean I could go out and buy an old speedometer, and change it to mph?  <P>P.S.  The main thing I am worrying about is the odometer.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||04-08-2000||08:34 PM||||You can turn the odometer manually.  You have to do each cylinder individually and you have to go forward.  There's something on the back of the odometer that needs to be released 1st.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||04-08-2000||08:46 PM||||If I turn it, won't there be little silver indicator lines between the numbers?||||reg||10
Z||000005||Formula||04-08-2000||08:48 PM||||If you go to austrailia and flush a toilet the water spins the wrong direction....<P>Weird||||reg||1
Z||000006||N_Man||04-08-2000||09:35 PM||||I dont know if its the same on an 85.<BR>But I live in Canada. Drive an 87GT with a KPH dash and it has miles on the inside of the km's.<P>If you just want to look at miles sorry for that.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ezsurf||04-10-2000||09:42 AM||||Fropuff,<BR>To convert to mph, simply divide km by 1.609344.  Most people use 1.6 or 1.61 to convert to mph. It all depends on how exact you want to be.  - ez||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||04-11-2000||09:28 AM||||Formula, As long as the water spins <I>downward</I> I think you'll be Ok.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Carrolles||04-12-2000||07:28 AM||||I believe you can pop the odometer out and swap it into the new speedometer.||||reg||1
